  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#obtain-a-physical-form says:\r\n\r\n> When the user actually obtains a physical form (or a representation of a physical form) of a Document, the user agent is expected to create a new rendering of the Document for the print media.\r\n\r\nIn practice, Chrome switches the existing document and its Window to the \"print\" medium (in terms of matchMedia listeners firing, etc), then switches them back.  Firefox creates a snapshot of the existing Document and prints _that_, and doesn't do anything to the Window.  I haven't tested what other UAs do.\r\n\r\nIt would be good to figure out something interoperable here.  Note that in practice printing needs to proceed while the actual document is still visible, which is not really a thing the web platform supports well when there is only one Document.",
